# f1 = owner, f4 = steps, f5 = first, f6 = second, f2 = ownerOfAsync, f7 = waits, f8 = third, f9 = fourth
# A call of a generator function reads the prototype of the function that is called, and the object it makes has that prototype. So a generator function that inner functions alone call is one function a run of its owner: no inner function makes it anew where it reads its name. An async generator function is one too. A plain function that is only called may still be made where it is read: nobody can tell.
